questions.stem_md:
The warden of an imagined hostel wants to keep room records in MySQL. Write SQL commands to:

(i) create a database named `hostel`;
(ii) open it for use;
(iii) create a table `ROOM` with columns `RoomNo` (integer, primary key), `Block` (one character) and `Beds` (integer);
(iv) add a column `Floor` (integer) to `ROOM`;
(v) remove the primary key from `ROOM`, and then see the structure of the table.

answer.model_answer_md:
```sql
CREATE DATABASE hostel;
USE hostel;
CREATE TABLE ROOM (RoomNo INT PRIMARY KEY, Block CHAR(1), Beds INT);
ALTER TABLE ROOM ADD Floor INT;
ALTER TABLE ROOM DROP PRIMARY KEY;
DESCRIBE ROOM;
```

One mark for each of (i) to (v); in (v), DESCRIBE (or DESC) shows the columns, now without a key on RoomNo.
